      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/claude-confident-hypatia-6g67t9-repin-bootstrap/cat-harness/process/Process_SubscribeKg",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns/Process",
      "name": "Subscribe to an external knowledge graph",
      "summary": "Subscribe a folio or harness to an external knowledge graph pinned to a full commit SHA, then take each chosen part from referenced to materialized through `materialize-remote` and instantiate each chosen harness once its needs are held, so the harness appear…",
      "description": "Subscribe a folio or harness to an external knowledge graph pinned to a full commit SHA, then take each chosen part from referenced to materialized through `materialize-remote` and instantiate each chosen harness once its needs are held, so the harness appears in the subscriber's navbar.\n\nA SUBSCRIPTION IS NOT A NEW MECHANISM, and this diagram is where that claim is kept honest. Every byte that arrives does so through Process_MaterializeRemote, called once per chosen subgraph or asset; every held copy is refreshed through Process_RefreshMaterialized. Neither is re-described here. What this process adds is only the walk: pin, validate, choose, and then carry each chosen part from referenced to materialised one at a time.\n\nA SUBSTRATE is a repository whose root declaration meets bootstrap's schema requirements and declares at least one harness. Both are answerable from the declaration file alone, so validating one never needs the whole repository.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES: processes/library/, beside Process_MaterializeRemote and Process_RefreshMaterialized, which it calls, naming the kg-subscription and materialize-remote skills in skills/library/large-datasets/; every ref stays inside the harness.\n\nSTRICT. The pin and the five gates are the reason: an unpinned subscription is how two subscribers see two graphs under one name, and a gate that only warned is a gate nobody fails.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "processes/library/subscribe-kg.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness/blob/main/processes/library/subscribe-kg.bpmn",
